From 3f84cf464e6dffec159b44156df95cb2fe0573d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarqaterge <omarqaterge@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:17:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): keep the prompt a model-switch marker
 absorbed when the next switch strips it

The model-switch marker is a role=user row (#48338), so the next real prompt
forms a user;user pair that alternation repair folds into it in place
("<marker>\n\n<prompt>"), and that merged dict becomes the live session
history. The next switch's dedup drops every entry that starts with the
marker prefix, so it deleted the absorbed prompt too: the transcript still
shows it, but the model never sees it again. Switching before the first
message loses the opening prompt (the payload then leads with an assistant
turn, #131382); switching mid-chat loses the message sent right after the
previous switch.

The dedup now keeps a merged entry as a copy holding only the absorbed text.
The mid-turn switch reconciliation in _commit_turn_history compares both
sides through the same strip, so a switch during the next turn still
commits it.

Refs #131382
